# How to use consent

| Package | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `@nu-art/consent-shared` | `ConsentStore`, `ConsentSource`, `DefaultConsentCategories`, category constants |
| `@nu-art/consent-frontend` | `ModuleFE_Consent`, `Component_ConsentBanner`, `ModulePackFE_Consent` |

## Wiring

```typescript
import {ModulePackFE_Consent, Component_ConsentBanner} from '@nu-art/consent-frontend';

.addModules(...ModulePackFE_Consent)

// Frontend config
ModuleFE_Consent: {privacyPolicyUrl: 'https://example.com/privacy', policyVersion: 1}

// Once, at the app root
<Component_ConsentBanner texts={{acceptAll: t('consent.accept'), ...}}/>
```

App-defined categories: set `categories: [...DefaultConsentCategories, {key: 'video-embeds'}]`.

## Gating third parties

```typescript
ModuleFE_Consent.subscribe('video-embeds', granted => granted ? loadPlayer() : unloadPlayer());
if (ModuleFE_Consent.isGranted('video-embeds')) loadPlayer();
```

`subscribe` fires on changes only. Read `isGranted` once at startup.

## Rules

- Consent-aware libraries take a `ConsentSource` (from consent-shared). They never import consent-frontend; the app passes `ModuleFE_Consent`.
- Never load a non-necessary script, cookie or pixel before `isGranted` is true.
- Keep Accept and Reject equal: do not restyle one of them.
- Bump `policyVersion` when you add purposes or vendors.
- Link a "Cookie settings" entry to `ModuleFE_Consent.openSettings()` so consent can be withdrawn.
